  "gross_volume_note": "Sum of constructed cells before drills and overlap removal. Excludes primary/frame feature bodies. This is an upper bound, not an aircraft BOM.",
  "issues": [
    "7500 lb is the user assumption. The 3.8g/-1.5g envelope and 70/30 roll split have not been established from the aircraft mission, design speeds, control inputs or gusts.",
    "The local sizing envelope applies the heavy roll-wing load to the symmetric pair and omits wing-mass inertial relief. Symmetric structure must withstand either roll direction, but this does not mean both wings have the heavy-side load simultaneously.",
    "All elastic buckling capacities are multiplied by 0.65 and then required to exceed 1.15 times ultimate demand. These additional allowances are not calibrated to an imperfection or restraint model.",
    "The no-buckling-at-ultimate criterion excludes postbuckling reserve. That reserve cannot be credited without a suitable nonlinear panel model and validation.",
    "76 mm cap width is retained to accommodate root fasteners across the span. It was not optimized as a spanwise width distribution.",
    "Center covers, bulkhead depth, residual floors, frame sections and large full-chord splice plates retain proposed minima or fixed dimensions; the wing gauge search does not optimize them.",
    "The global mass includes finite dense attachment beams and approximate primary rings. Those masses are analysis idealizations, not measured manufactured parts.",
    "Projected thin-wall section formulas do not exactly reproduce the native stock intersections. Cap/web/cover overlap and gauge conventions need reconciliation for both mass and stiffness.",
    "The global model credits perfect skin attachment and unresolved center-box stiffeners. It also concentrates tail loads at simplified equivalent attachments. These assumptions can be optimistic locally.",
    "The discrete gauge search is a local search. It does not prove minimum weight or optimum rib and stringer spacing."
  ]
}
